# Egress allowlist for the Iris sandbox (POSIX extended regex, one per line).
# Matched against the destination host of every request, including HTTPS CONNECT.
# Anything not matched here is blocked. Edit, then: docker restart iris-proxy
#
# Anthropic / Claude Code — API, auth/login (platform.claude.com), and
# server-side WebSearch/WebFetch.
(^|\.)anthropic\.com$
(^|\.)claude\.ai$
(^|\.)claude\.com$
# Python packaging — pip (PyPI + its file CDN).
(^|\.)pypi\.org$
(^|\.)pythonhosted\.org$
# Node packaging — npm registry.
(^|\.)npmjs\.org$
(^|\.)npmjs\.com$
# Rust packaging — cargo (crates.io API/index + the crate CDN) and rustup
# component/toolchain fetches (static.rust-lang.org).
(^|\.)crates\.io$
(^|\.)rust-lang\.org$
# Playwright browser downloads (the e2e suite installs headless chromium). If a
# download is refused, add the host name Playwright prints to this list.
(^|\.)playwright\.dev$
# GitHub — read-only fetch/clone, release assets, raw content. NOTE: no git
# credentials are mounted, so this permits reads only; the agent cannot push.
(^|\.)github\.com$
(^|\.)githubusercontent\.com$
